spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "On a Safari", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A safari is a trip to observe wild animals, especially in Africa. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about a safari, you use the verb \u201cto go\u201d: <br>--<span class=\"italic\">I went on a safari last year. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You talk about the different animals, for example:<br> --<span class=\"italic\">I saw many lions or I didn't see a cheetah.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can talk about the geographic features:<br> -- <span class=\"italic\">I saw a large mountain!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about geographic features, you can use a variety of adjectives to describe them, for example:<span class=\"italic\"> --stunning, breathtaking, spectacular, beautiful.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you're talking to someone about a safari you went on, they can ask questions like:<br><span class=\"italic\">-- What did you see?<br> --Did you take pictures?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Comparatives and Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use adjectives to compare two things. These are called  <span class=\"strong\">comparative</span> adjectives. You can also use adjectives to compare one item with the rest of a group. These are called <span class=\"strong\">superlative</span> adjectives.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The lion is smaller than the tiger.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " For regular comparative adjectives, you can use the structure:  <br/> <ul><li> adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-er</span>) <span class=\"strong\">than</span><br/>  Use this when the adjective in question is a short, one-syllable word.<br/> e.g. <span class=\"italic\">small &#8594; smaller</span></li> <li>adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-ier</span>) <span class=\"strong\">than</span><br/>  Use this if the adjective ends in <span class=\"italic\">-y</span> and has two syllables.<br/> e.g. <span class=\"italic\">happy &#8594; happier</span></li> <li><span class=\"strong\">more/less</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">than</span><br/> Use this if the adjective has 2 or more syllables. The adjective does not change. <br/> e.g. <span class=\"italic\">careful &#8594; more careful</span>, <span class=\"italic\">boring &#8594; less boring</span><br/> There are a few exceptions, however: <span class=\"italic\">simple &#8594; simpler</span>, <span class=\"italic\">narrow  &#8594; narrower</span></li> <li><span class=\"strong\">as</span> + adjective + <span class=\"strong\">as</span> <br/> Use this when comparing two things that are the same regarding the adjective in question. The adjective does not change.<br/> e.g. <span class=\"italic\">I'm as fast as you. </span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>For regular superlative adjectives, you can use the structure:<br/>  <ul><li> <span class=\"strong\">the</span> adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-est</span>)<br/> Use this when the adjective in question is a short, one-syllable word.<br/> e.g. <span class=\"italic\">small &#8594; smallest</span></li> <li><span class=\"strong\">the</span> adjective (<span class=\"strong\">-iest</span>)<br/> Use this if the word ends in <span class=\"italic\">-y</span> and has two syllables.<br/> e.g. <span class=\"italic\">happy &#8594; happiest</span> <br></li> <li><span class=\"strong\">the most/least</span> + adjective <br/>Use this if the adjective has 2 or more syllables. The adjective does not change.<br/> e.g. <span class=\"italic\">careful &#8594; most careful</span>, <span class=\"italic\">boring &#8594; most boring</span><br/> There are a few exceptions, however: <span class=\"italic\">simple &#8594; simplest</span>, <span class=\"italic\">narrow &#8594; narrowest</span></li></ul> </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The cheetah is the fastest animal in the cat family.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was the best trip!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are some irregular adjectives that do not follow these rules. Please look at the chart below to find the comparative and superlative forms for common irregular adjectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Comparative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"better\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"best\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"worse\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"worst\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"little\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"less\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"least\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"much\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"most\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"far\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"further / farther\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"furthest / farthest\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rhino ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "short form for rhinoceros, a large animal with thick skin and one or two horns   ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We saw a grey rhino.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about things you see when traveling.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dinosaur ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of reptiles that lived millions of years ago ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rhinos look like dinosaurs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "horn", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pointed part that grows on the heads of some animals ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Rhinos get hunted for their horns.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "buffalo ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an animal similar to a large cow with long curved horns ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We also saw some buffaloes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mammal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a type of animal that drinks milk from its mother's body when it is young.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Rhinos are mammals like humans.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mud bath", "type": "name"}, {"content": "putting your body in mud ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The hippos like to take mud baths.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hippo", "type": "name"}, {"content": "short for hippopotamus, a large animal with a big head and mouth that lives near water  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There was a family of hippos walking around.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to snap a photo", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to photograph something quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I snapped a photo of the moment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go on the Internet to research about rhinos and hippos. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Fill out the table about hippos and rhinos.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph (6-7 sentences) using the information from your table.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Rhino\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hippo\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What  does it look like?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Where does it  live?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"How long does it  live?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research rhinos and hippos.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I fill out a table.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare rhinos and hippos. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I proofread my paragraph.", "type": "text"}]}]}